  <h1>Simple Explain Nitro Cold Brew Coffee</h1>
  <p class="muted">The live page is an interactive guide. This static version keeps its explanatory content; the interactive questions and branching are not yet rebuilt.</p>

  <h2>If You Are a First Time Nitro / Cold Brew Consumer, Welcome!</h2>
  <p>The guide first asks whether you have experience with draft, nitro or cold brew serving, and routes experienced and first-time visitors to different explanations.</p>

  <h2>What Is Nitro Coffee - Draft Cold Brew Coffee Dispense From Tap</h2>
  <p>Nitro coffee is cold brew coffee kegged and pressurized with nitrogen, then served from a draft tap.</p>

  <p>Related terms you may know it by: cold brew on draft, nitro draft coffee, draft nitro coffee, cold brew draft, and the coffee draft system that dispenses it.</p>

  <h2>How much do you plan to serve?</h2>
  <p>The guide then asks about scale and serving volume, and moves into guidance for small businesses, offices and shops. See <a href="/kegerators/">equipment to serve nitro coffee</a>, <a href="/nitro-coffee-kegs/">nitro coffee kegs</a> and <a href="/howtobuy/">how to buy</a>, or <a href="/contact-bona-fide-nitro-coffee-and-tea/">contact us</a>.</p>
